  "findings": [
    "v1 exposed reuse of the one native-stack lease per HostCall across multiple raw scans; each scan now runs in a distinct nested host callback.",
    "v2 failed to compile because UTF-8 error construction overlapped a borrowed stack slice; validation now ends the slice borrow before building the VM error.",
    "v3 passed four cases and failed three: effect setter deltas were missing from command capture, the queue fixture had not ended startup discovery, and fatal entry abort prevented nested restoration callbacks.",
    "Effect setter deltas now pass through the shared capture writer in existing target order, retaining normal frame/message publication while also recording command blocks.",
    "Queue fixture now completes the actual native and Rust startup discovery before invoking nested queued commands; its output and shared-state assertions remain intact.",
    "Snapshot setup, authored execution, and restoration now use separate top-level VM entries. Fatal instruction abort is not bypassed or weakened in the engine.",
    "v4 failed to compile when pinning a returned value while the VM return slice was borrowed; the first Value is now copied before pinning.",
    "v5 passed all eight focused cases; an additional weak-value GC case verifies retention of only the first Lua return through restoration, then release.",
    "Final source uses the existing lifecycle plan invalidation routine, releasing registry roots when restored state invalidates traversal plans.",
    "Capture reset preserves preexisting semantic queue steps; direct helper intentionally does not restore script globals, upvalues, RNG, or unrelated actors. Those belong to the caller outer probe scope.",
    "Preparation clock follows the native boundary: snapshot/setup errors may leave the selected beat, while callback errors restore semantic state and then prior runtime values.",
    "No failing coverage removed, weakened, or ignored; original 80 activation tests remain an exact prefix.",
    "Current regression durations are verification costs, not representative preparation/live/memory measurements."
